WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.700
Audio passes through transcription, decision and synthesis. Each boundary changes its representation.

2
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:14.700
Text makes stages inspectable and replaceable, but does not retain every acoustic signal.

3
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:23.000
The same turn crosses every stage. The runtime must coordinate their results.

4
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:30.700
An audio-native model receives speech directly, without requiring a transcript first.

5
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:37.700
When it returns text only, an external voice can synthesize the response.

6
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:46.000
Input prosody does not automatically reach TTS. That boundary needs an explicit contract.

7
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:53.700
Speech-to-speech connects input and output audio without a mandatory text boundary.

8
00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:00.700
The acoustic path becomes simpler; tools and their permissions remain outside the model.

9
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:09.000
The application validates the action. A speaking model does not gain business authority.

10
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:16.700
Accepting and generating audio does not imply listening and speaking simultaneously.

11
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:23.700
With full-duplex, input and output can coexist. The system decides how to handle overlap.

12
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:32.000
Modality and turn control are different decisions. S2S does not guarantee full-duplex.

13
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:39.700
A browser can send media directly to a provider while the backend keeps control.

14
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:46.700
Removing a framework does not remove authentication, state, tools or recovery.

15
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:55.000
Draw the actual path and give every transition an owner.

16
00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:02.700
An explicit transcript favors a cascade; an external voice needs its own boundary.

17
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:09.700
When acoustic information matters, test audio-native input on the same task.

18
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:18.000
Compare task success, voice and reliability under equal conditions. No architecture wins universally.

